From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:09:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: hfi_cmds: accept the H.264 8x8 transform
 property on HFI v3

venc_set_properties() sets HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8 for
every H.264 session, but only the 4xx packetization knows the property.
On HFI v3 (msm8996) it falls through to the 1x code, which returns
-EINVAL, so encoder queue setup fails and VIDIOC_REQBUFS returns EINVAL:
H.264 encoding does not work at all.

The v3 firmware supports the property (the downstream msm_vidc driver
for msm8996 sends HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_8X8_TRANSFORM, same ID,
as a plain enable), so pack it the same way as on v4.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096, VIDEO.VE.4.4-00060).

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
index 3ae063094e..9684ecb5f4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -1177,6 +1177,13 @@ pkt_session_set_property_3xx(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *pkt,
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VDEC_CONTINUE_DATA_TRANSFER:
 		/* for 3xx fw version session_continue is used */
 		break;
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8: {
+		struct hfi_h264_8x8_transform *in = pdata, *tm = prop_data;
+
+		tm->enable_type = in->enable_type;
+		pkt->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32) + sizeof(*tm);
+		break;
+	}
 	default:
 		ret = pkt_session_set_property_1x(pkt, cookie, ptype, pdata);
 		break;
